{%- comment -%}
  main-product — the product page. One section, branching on product type.

  Built 31/08/2026, plain wedding rings first. The other types are stubbed at
  the branch, not written: they get the shared shell (gallery, buy box, spec,
  guarantees) and their own buy-box include as each is built.

  NOT PORTED FROM LIVE'S MARKUP. Live's main-product is 162KB of T4S and shares
  its buy box with main-qv; it could not be read whole even if it were worth
  copying. This is built from the DATA instead, which is unambiguous — see
  below — and from the design system. Ed's call: improve where live is weak.

  ── THE DATA MODEL, which drives every decision here ──────────────────────

  A plain wedding ring is ONE PRODUCT PER combination of metal, profile, width
  and weight. Its variants are RING SIZES ONLY: 70 of them, A to Z+9.5, priced
  in steps as the size goes up.

    options            Ring Size (the only one)
    custom.ring_metal    "14ct Yellow Gold"
    custom.ring_profile  "Concave"
    custom.ring_width    2.0            (number_decimal)
    custom.ring_weight   "Heavy Weight"
    custom.ring_type     ["Plain Wedding Ring"]
    custom.spin_360      a Sirv .spin URL
    filters.band_width   "2mm"          (the string form; see the slug note)

  So SIZE is a variant picker and METAL IS NAVIGATION — choosing a different
  metal means going to a different product. That is not a quirk to work around;
  it is the catalogue's shape, and the buy box has to be honest about it.

  ── HOW THE METAL SWITCHER FINDS ITS SIBLINGS ─────────────────────────────

  Handles are perfectly systematic, verified against live 31/08/2026:

      {metal}-{profile}-wedding-ring-{width}-{weight}
      14ct-yellow-gold-concave-wedding-ring-2mm-heavy
      18ct-white-gold-concave-wedding-ring-2mm-heavy
      platinum-concave-wedding-ring-25mm-medium

  so the ten metal siblings are CONSTRUCTED and looked up with all_products.
  No app, no metafield list of references, no JS. Two things follow:

    · `all_products` is capped at TWENTY unique handles per page. Ten metals
      fits. Adding profile (9), width (many) or weight (4) switchers the same
      way would blow straight through it — those need a different mechanism,
      so do not "just add one more row" here.
    · a handle that does not exist simply returns nothing and that metal is
      rendered as unavailable. A missing combination degrades to a greyed
      swatch rather than a dead link, which is the failure we want.

  The width slug is the one irregular part: 2.5mm appears in handles as "25mm",
  not "2-5mm", so it comes from `filters.band_width | remove: '.'` rather than
  from the `handle` filter, which would produce "2-5mm" and 404.

  ── STILL OPEN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  custom.spin_360 holds a Sirv 360 spin for every plain band. Rendering it
  needs Sirv's viewer script — a third-party script in a theme that has one JS
  file by design — so it is NOT wired up. The hook is marked in the gallery.
  Ed's decision.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign p = product
  assign cf = p.metafields.custom

  comment
    Which branch. ring_type is a list metafield, so `first`. Falls back to the
    product type, then to a generic layout — a product with neither still
    renders a correct page, just without the type-specific extras.
  endcomment
  assign ring_type = cf.ring_type.value | first | default: p.type
  assign is_plain = false
  if ring_type contains 'Plain Wedding'
    assign is_plain = true
  endif

  assign current = p.selected_or_first_available_variant

  comment
    Sibling handles. The three parts that stay fixed across metals.
  endcomment
  assign profile_slug = cf.ring_profile | handle
  assign width_slug = p.metafields.filters.band_width | remove: '.'
  assign weight_slug = cf.ring_weight | split: ' ' | first | downcase

  assign metal_names = '9ct Yellow Gold,9ct White Gold,9ct Rose Gold,14ct Yellow Gold,14ct White Gold,14ct Rose Gold,18ct Yellow Gold,18ct White Gold,18ct Rose Gold,Platinum' | split: ','
  assign metal_tokens = 'gem,gem,gem' | split: ','
-%}

<section class="band band--white pdp" data-screen-label="Product">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="pdp__top">

      {%- comment -%} ---- Gallery ---- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pdp__gallery">
        {%- comment -%}
          360 SPIN HOOK. cf.spin_360 is a Sirv .spin URL present on every plain
          band. Rendering it requires Sirv's viewer script; not wired up
          pending a decision on adding a third-party script. When it is, it
          becomes the FIRST slide here, not a replacement for the stills.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if p.media.size > 0 -%}
          <div class="pdp__stage">
            {{ p.featured_media | image_url: width: 1400 | image_tag:
               loading: 'eager',
               widths: '400,600,900,1200,1400',
               sizes: '(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 55vw',
               alt: p.featured_media.alt | default: p.title,
               class: 'pdp__hero' }}
          </div>

          {%- if p.media.size > 1 -%}
            <ul class="pdp__thumbs">
              {%- for media in p.media limit: 8 -%}
                <li>
                  <a class="pdp__thumb" href="{{ media | image_url: width: 1400 }}">
                    {{ media | image_url: width: 200 | image_tag:
                       loading: 'lazy',
                       widths: '100,200',
                       sizes: '80px',
                       alt: '' }}
                  </a>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- else -%}
          <div class="pdp__stage pdp__stage--empty"></div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} ---- Buy box ---- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pdp__buy">

        {%- if cf.ring_metal != blank -%}
          <p class="eyebrow">{{ cf.ring_metal }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <h1 class="pdp__title">{{ p.title }}</h1>

        <p class="pdp__price">
          <span class="pdp__now">{{ current.price | money }}</span>
          {%- if current.compare_at_price > current.price -%}
            <s class="pdp__was">{{ current.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>

        {%- if is_plain -%}
          <p class="pdp__pricenote fine">Price shown is for size {{ current.title }}. Larger sizes use more metal and cost a little more.</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          ---- Metal: navigation, not a variant ----
          Ten constructed handles. An absent combination renders as a disabled
          swatch, so the row always shows the full range and tells the truth
          about what we make.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if is_plain and profile_slug != blank and width_slug != blank and weight_slug != blank -%}
          <div class="pdp__field">
            <p class="pdp__label">Metal<span class="pdp__labelval">{{ cf.ring_metal }}</span></p>
            <ul class="pdp__metals">
              {%- for name in metal_names -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign metal_slug = name | handle
                  assign sib_handle = metal_slug | append: '-' | append: profile_slug | append: '-wedding-ring-' | append: width_slug | append: '-' | append: weight_slug
                  assign sib = all_products[sib_handle]
                  assign is_current = false
                  if name == cf.ring_metal
                    assign is_current = true
                  endif
                  assign swatch_token = name | handle | prepend: '--metal-' | replace: '--metal-9ct-', '--metal-9-' | replace: '--metal-14ct-', '--metal-14-' | replace: '--metal-18ct-', '--metal-18-' | replace: '-gold', ''
                -%}
                <li>
                  {%- if is_current -%}
                    <span class="pdp__metal is-current" style="--sw: var({{ swatch_token }});" aria-current="true">
                      <span class="pdp__swatch"></span>
                      <span class="visually-hidden">{{ name }}, selected</span>
                    </span>
                  {%- elsif sib != blank -%}
                    <a class="pdp__metal" href="{{ sib.url }}" style="--sw: var({{ swatch_token }});">
                      <span class="pdp__swatch"></span>
                      <span class="visually-hidden">{{ name }} — {{ sib.price_min | money }}</span>
                    </a>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <span class="pdp__metal is-off" style="--sw: var({{ swatch_token }});">
                      <span class="pdp__swatch"></span>
                      <span class="visually-hidden">{{ name }}, not made in this profile and width</span>
                    </span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} ---- The form: size, engraving, add to bag ---- {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- form 'product', p, class: 'pdp__form', id: 'pdp-form' -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ current.id }}" data-fye-variant-id>

          {%- if p.has_only_default_variant == false -%}
            {%- for option in p.options_with_values -%}
              <div class="pdp__field">
                <label class="pdp__label" for="pdp-opt-{{ forloop.index }}">
                  {{ option.name }}
                  {%- if option.name == 'Ring Size' -%}
                    <a class="pdp__sizelink" href="{{ s.size_guide_url | default: '/pages/ring-size-guide' }}">Find my size</a>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </label>
                <select class="pdp__select"
                        id="pdp-opt-{{ forloop.index }}"
                        name="options[{{ option.name | escape }}]"
                        data-fye-option="{{ forloop.index }}">
                  {%- for value in option.values -%}
                    <option value="{{ value | escape }}"{% if option.selected_value == value %} selected{% endif %}>{{ value }}</option>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if s.engraving -%}
            <div class="pdp__field">
              <label class="pdp__label" for="pdp-engraving">
                {{ s.engraving_label | default: 'Engraving' }}
                <span class="pdp__labelnote">Optional</span>
              </label>
              <input class="pdp__input"
                     type="text"
                     id="pdp-engraving"
                     name="properties[{{ s.engraving_label | default: 'Engraving' | escape }}]"
                     maxlength="{{ s.engraving_max | default: 30 }}"
                     placeholder="{{ s.engraving_placeholder | escape }}">
              <p class="pdp__hint fine">{{ s.engraving_hint }}</p>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          <button class="btn btn--block pdp__atc" type="submit" name="add"{% unless current.available %} disabled{% endunless %}>
            {%- if current.available -%}
              {{ s.atc_label | default: 'Add to bag' }}
            {%- else -%}
              Made to order — enquire
            {%- endif -%}
          </button>
        {%- endform -%}

        {%- if s.reassurance != blank -%}
          <p class="pdp__reassure fine">{{ s.reassurance }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} ---- Spec: straight from the metafields ---- {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if is_plain -%}
          <dl class="pdp__spec">
            {%- if cf.ring_metal != blank -%}
              <div class="pdp__specrow"><dt>Metal</dt><dd>{{ cf.ring_metal }}</dd></div>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if cf.ring_profile != blank -%}
              <div class="pdp__specrow"><dt>Profile</dt><dd>{{ cf.ring_profile }}</dd></div>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if p.metafields.filters.band_width != blank -%}
              <div class="pdp__specrow"><dt>Width</dt><dd>{{ p.metafields.filters.band_width }}</dd></div>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if cf.ring_weight != blank -%}
              <div class="pdp__specrow"><dt>Weight</dt><dd>{{ cf.ring_weight }}</dd></div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </dl>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- if p.description != blank -%}
      <div class="pdp__desc prose">{{ p.description }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
.fye .pdp__top {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;
  gap: var(--s10);
  align-items: start;
}

/* --- gallery ------------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .pdp__stage {
  background: var(--ivory);
}

.fye .pdp__hero {
  width: 100%;
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  object-fit: cover;
}

.fye .pdp__stage--empty {
  aspect-ratio: 1;
}

.fye .pdp__thumbs {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: var(--s2);
  margin: var(--s2) 0 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.fye .pdp__thumbs > li {
  margin: 0;
}

.fye .pdp__thumb {
  display: block;
  width: 80px;
  background: var(--ivory);
  border: 1px solid transparent;
}

.fye .pdp__thumb:hover {
  border-color: var(--sage);
}

/* --- buy box ------------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .pdp__buy {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s5);
}

.fye .pdp__title {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-h2);
}

.fye .pdp__price {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: var(--s3);
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-h4);
}

.fye .pdp__now {
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
}

.fye .pdp__was {
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
}

.fye .pdp__pricenote {
  margin: calc(var(--s5) * -1 + var(--s2)) 0 0;
}

.fye .pdp__field {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s2);
}

.fye .pdp__label {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s4);
  margin: 0;
}

/* The chosen value sits in the label rather than only in the control, so the
   selection is readable without opening a 70-item select. */
.fye .pdp__labelval {
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
  letter-spacing: 0;
  text-transform: none;
  color: var(--ink);
}

.fye .pdp__labelnote {
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
  letter-spacing: 0;
  text-transform: none;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__sizelink {
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
  letter-spacing: 0;
  text-transform: none;
  border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
}

/* --- metal swatches ------------------------------------------------------ */

.fye .pdp__metals {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: var(--s2);
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.fye .pdp__metals > li {
  margin: 0;
}

.fye .pdp__metal {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 44px;
  height: 44px;
  border: 1px solid transparent;
}

.fye .pdp__swatch {
  display: block;
  width: 28px;
  height: 28px;
  background: var(--sw);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--gem-edge);
}

.fye .pdp__metal:hover {
  border-color: var(--sage);
}

.fye .pdp__metal.is-current {
  border-color: var(--line-strong);
}

/* Not made in this profile and width. Shown rather than hidden, so the row
   always states the full range. */
.fye .pdp__metal.is-off {
  opacity: 0.35;
  cursor: not-allowed;
}

/* --- form ---------------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .pdp__form {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s5);
  margin: 0;
}

.fye .pdp__select,
.fye .pdp__input {
  width: 100%;
}

.fye .pdp__hint {
  margin: 0;
}

.fye .pdp__reassure {
  margin: 0;
}

/* --- spec ---------------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .pdp__spec {
  margin: 0;
  padding-top: var(--s5);
  border-top: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .pdp__specrow {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s4);
  padding: var(--s3) 0;
  border-bottom: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .pdp__specrow dt {
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__specrow dd {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
}

/* --- description --------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .pdp__desc {
  margin-top: var(--s10);
}

/* --- breakpoints. Media queries LAST, always. ---------------------------- */

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .fye .pdp__top {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--s7);
  }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Main product",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "fye-main-product",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Buy box" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "atc_label", "label": "Add to bag label", "default": "Add to bag" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "size_guide_url", "label": "Ring size guide" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "reassurance",
      "label": "Reassurance line",
      "default": "Handmade to order in the UK. Free delivery, complimentary resizing for a year."
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Engraving" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "engraving", "label": "Offer engraving", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "engraving_label", "label": "Field label", "default": "Engraving" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "engraving_placeholder", "label": "Placeholder", "default": "A date, a name, a few words" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "engraving_max",
      "label": "Maximum characters",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "ch",
      "default": 30
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "engraving_hint",
      "label": "Helper text",
      "default": "Engraved inside the band. Free of charge, and it does not affect delivery time."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Main product" }]
}
{% endschema %}
